<article class="env-lemma" id="035A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/035A">Lemma <span data-tag="035A">29.18.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism. If $S$ is Nagata and $f$ locally of finite type then $X$ is Nagata. If $S$ is universally Japanese and $f$ locally of finite type then $X$ is universally Japanese. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For “universally Japanese” this follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/032S" data-tag="032S">10.162.4</a>. For “Nagata” this follows from Algebra, Proposition <a href="/tag/0334" data-tag="0334">10.162.15</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>